# Marks the root of a SerenStarwright checkout.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Starwright used to find its repo by walking up looking
# for a directory named "Bash/". That broke twice - once inside a zipapp (where
# __file__ resolves to the archive itself, so there is no directory to find),
# once on a box with no checkout at all - and the reorg into services/ + nodes/
# would have broken it a third time, because the directory names it sniffed for
# were exactly the thing being renamed.
#
# An explicit marker makes the layout something the repo DECLARES rather than a
# convention the tooling has memorised. Rename any directory below and update
# one line here; nothing else needs to know.
#
# Resolution order in seren-starwright.py:
#   1. $SEREN_STARWRIGHT_ROOT   - explicit operator override
#   2. walk up for this file    - normal checkout
#   3. copy bundled in the .pyz - single-file deploy on a bare box
#
# Parsed with a deliberately dumb key = value reader (no toml dependency on a
# fresh Jetson). Values are paths relative to this file.

# The repo uses the nested Visual Studio layout the rest of the Seren stack
# uses - solution and solution-items at the top, the project one level down:
#
#   SerenStarwright/              <- this file, .slnx, LICENSE, README, .github
#   SerenStarwright/SerenStarwright/   <- the .pyproj and everything it owns
#
# So the marker stays at the TRUE repo root (where .git and the README live,
# which is what "root" should mean) and points inward. This is precisely the
# edit this file exists to make cheap: a reorg costs two lines here instead of
# a code change and a re-test.
services = SerenStarwright/services
nodes    = SerenStarwright/nodes
